  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A small string shopper bag is a 30 × 35 cm market bag in DK cotton worked in ch-2 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "mesh construction",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mesh-construction"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": two flat mesh panels joined at the sides with a sl st seam, with twisted chain handles at the top. Strong enough for a standard small grocery shop. One 100 m ball of DK cotton makes one bag."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "slug": "crochet-hook",
              "label": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "tapestry-needle",
              "label": "Tapestry needle",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "craft-scissors",
              "label": "Scissors",
              "isOptional": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "100 m DK cotton string or cotton twine. One 100 m ball makes one bag."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each ch-2 mesh square = approx. 1.3 × 1.3 cm in DK cotton string with a 4 mm hook. The bag body is 23 mesh squares wide × 27 mesh rows tall = approx. 30 × 35 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc). UK term; US equivalent is single crochet (sc). connecting stitch between mesh spaces."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr). UK term; US equivalent is double crochet (dc). Used for the top border row."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bag panel (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 72."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Row 1: 1 dc in 6th ch from hook, *ch 2, skip 2 ch, 1 dc in next ch; repeat from * across (23 mesh sps). Turn."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "All rows: ch 4 (t-ch, counts as dc + ch 2), *1 dc in dc of prev row, ch 2; repeat from * ending 1 dc in t-ch (23 mesh sps). Turn."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Work 27 rows. On the final row, work a solid top border: ch 1, 2 dc into each ch-2 sp and 1 dc into each dc across (69 dc). Fasten off."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hold both panels WS together. Sl st through both back loops down each side edge and across the bottom to close the bag. Fasten off at each join."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handles (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 90. Sl st back into the 1st ch to make a long loop. Twist the loop 4, 5 times to create a twisted rope handle. Attach each end of the handle to the top border of the bag: one end approx. 7 cm from each side edge. By folding over and stitching through with the tapestry needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. The bag stretches to hold produce and springs back when empty."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine-wash on 30°C gentle cycle in a mesh laundry bag. Hang to dry."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}